abstract: >-
  AI-assisted. Computer-assisted proofs (interval arithmetic, CAPD/MPFR) that timelike geodesics of the
  Manko–Novikov spacetime (M = 5, a = 3, one energy level) are chaotic: a transversal homoclinic orbit, hence
  positive topological entropy, at quadrupole deviation beta = 3/100; and a Melnikov-type theorem, with a certified
  first-order coefficient, for every 0 < |beta| < beta_0 (beta_0 not explicit), both signs. The decision arithmetic
  is re-evaluated in a second arithmetic library (Arb), and the field is independently re-derived from the published
  metric; these checks were done by separate AI sessions or systems, not human peer review. No entropy value is
  claimed. AI systems used: Claude (Anthropic) and Gemini (Google).
keywords:
  - computer-assisted proof
  - interval arithmetic
